<article class="env-lemma" id="0DI5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DI5">Lemma <span data-tag="0DI5">36.35.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is flat and locally of finite presentation. Let $g : S' \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Set $X' = S' \times _ S X$ and denote $g' : X' \to X$ the projection. If $K \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is $S$-perfect, then $L(g')^*K$ is $S'$-perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      First proof: reduce to the affine case using Lemma <a href="/tag/0DI2" data-tag="0DI2">36.35.3</a> and then apply More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DHW" data-tag="0DHW">15.85.5</a>. 
    <p>
      Second proof: $L(g')^*K$ is pseudo-coherent by Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/09U7" data-tag="09U7">20.47.3</a> and the bounded tor dimension property follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0C0V" data-tag="0C0V">36.22.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>